    <string name="open_note_from_outside_hint">To open a new note from outside Tratto:
• add the “New note” shortcut in Quick Settings;
• long-press the Tratto icon and drag “New note” to the home screen;
• to write on top of any app, use the quick note, with the Accessibility button;
• in Lawnchair: Home settings › Gestures › Double tap › App › Tratto (New note).</string>
    <string name="quick_note_blurb">A sheet for writing on top of any app. What you write joins your notes; if you close it without writing, nothing is kept.</string>
    <string name="quick_note_how_to">The simplest way: add the “%1$s” shortcut to Quick Settings (top shade, pencil to edit). Or in Accessibility, turn on “%2$s” and its shortcut: the Accessibility button (a floating button on screen) or both volume keys held. The service does not read the screen.
A double-click of the stylus button only works in Tratto: in other apps Android keeps it for itself, and listening to the stylus from outside would block it while you write.</string>
    <string name="restore_merge_replace_help">“Merge” adds the backup’s notes to yours: if a note exists on both sides, the newer version is kept and the other is saved as a copy.

“Replace” deletes the current notes and puts in the backup’s.</string>
    <string name="restore_finished">Restore finished: %1$s notes added, %2$s updated%3$s</string>
    <string name="restore_copies_suffix">, %1$s copies</string>
    <string name="lasso_help">Circle the strokes to move, resize, recolor or copy: images and text boxes come along. The handle at the bottom right resizes. A tap on an image or a box selects it.</string>
    <string name="text_box_help">Tap the page, with the stylus or a finger, to write in a text box; tap a box to edit it. With the stylus you can also drag sideways to set its width. The buttons above the keyboard change the style, font, colors, alignment and lists, as in Docs.</string>
    <string name="stylus_erase_tip">Tip: hold the stylus button while you write to erase. A long press, with the stylus above the page, opens the tool menu.</string>
    <string name="transcription_needs_recognition">Transcription needs handwriting recognition in the app\'s language: about 14 MB, downloaded once. After that it also works offline.</string>
    <string name="folder_backup_no_folder">No folder chosen. Tratto saves a .tratto file there, even every day, and keeps the last %1$s. A folder from an app that syncs, such as Nextcloud or Syncthing, works too. To restore, use “Restore from a file”.</string>
    <string name="google_oauth_not_configured">Google access is not set up for this app: Google Cloud Console needs an Android OAuth client with the right package and SHA-1.</string>
